# TODO - CPU VM table optimization

## Objective

Optimize scalar execution with precomputed rotate tables, position-dependent
decode tables, efficient crazy-operation decomposition, cheap pointer updates,
and benchmarked micro-optimizations without semantic drift.

## Current implementation

- `vm/build.rs` deterministically generates finite classic-profile rotate,
  five-trit crazy, positional-decode, and code-phase tables into Cargo-owned
  `OUT_DIR`; runtime initialization is not required.
- `Word::crazy` decomposes each ten-trit word into two five-trit chunks and uses
  one exact 243 by 243 table for each chunk position.
- `Word::rotate` uses a complete 59,049-entry table.
- Positional decode uses a 59,049-entry code-phase table plus a 94 by 94 decode
  table, avoiding repeated modulo work in the transition hot path.
- Exhaustive tests compare every rotate value, every five-trit crazy pair in
  both word positions, and every graphical-cell/code-pointer decode against
  independent scalar definitions.
- `benchmarks/interpreter/main.rs` emits raw nanosecond samples and deterministic
  checksums for scalar/table rotate and crazy paths. Post-commit evidence on
  `888b492` records 15 samples per implementation with 10.43x median speedup for
  crazy and 1.50x for rotate on the identified benchmark host.

## Acceptance

- Lookup tables or predecoded forms measurably reduce CPU work while
  exhaustive/property checks prove equality to the scalar rotate/crazy/decode
  definitions.
- Observable state, I/O, termination, and diagnostics match the declared
  semantic profile across positive, boundary, and adversarial fixtures.
- Performance conclusions use equivalent workloads and report raw-sample
  provenance, resource budgets, dispersion/uncertainty, and failure/success
  behavior rather than only a best-case number.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `vm/`, `execution/`, `tests/vm/`,
  `benchmarks/interpreter/`.
- Required evidence: semantic fixtures, state/I/O traces where diagnostic, and
  differential results against independent specification-conformant
  implementations; the historical interpreter is compared only on its documented
  agreement domain.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `safe-rust-malbolge-vm`.
- Performance evidence: `benchmarks/interpreter/evidence/2026-07-26-windows-x86_64/`
  retains raw samples, exact workload repetitions, checksums, commit identity,
  toolchain versions, host class, medians, dispersion summary, and scoped
  cleanliness at measurement time.
